In an increasingly complex world of development, keeping up-to-date with technologies and libraries is paramount. Here are some of my favorite open source .NET MVC libraries that help with authentication and authorization:

1. **OWIN** and **Katana** – OWIN (Open Web Interface for .NET) is a framework for all things related to web development, and a collection of open-source libraries developed on top of it that help in different aspects like authentication, authorization, etc.

2. **IdentityServer4** – IdentityServer4 is an OpenID Connect and OAuth 2.0 framework for ASP.NET Core, which is now being actively developed. It can also be used standalone as a secure token service where you can issue tokens as part of your authentication process.

3. **Auth0** – This service provides end-to-end identity, authentication and authorization as a service. It supports social identity providers and has SDKs for different platforms.

4. **AspNet.Security.OpenIdConnect.Server** and **IdentityServer3** – These are lightweight .NET libraries for developing OpenID Connect and OAuth 2.0 servers.

5. **ASP.NET Core Identity** – ASP.NET Core Identity is the new membership system included with ASP.NET Core and it also provides role-based authentication and role-based authorization.

6. **Microsoft.AspNet.Identity** – As the name suggests, it’s an implementation of ASP.NET Identities for older projects that still use the older versions of the AS--------------------            Debug.Assert(index >= Old_arrListIndexOfX && index <= Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);

            // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that if old count was equal to new count the order of the elements in old array was the same in new array
            if(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount && Old_arrListIndexOfX >=0 && New_arrListLastIndexOfX >=0)
                Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX == New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
            // assert that old arrList.contains(x) == new arrList.contains(x)
            Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListContainsX == New_arrListContainsX);

	    // assert that old arrList.IndexOf(x) == new arrList.IndexOf(x)
            Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListIndexOfX == New_arrListIndexOfX);

	    // assert that old arrList.LastIndexOf(x) == new arrList.LastIndexOf(x)
            Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
        }
    }
}

